  "response": "# Merge triage for `01-messy-ts-app` (39 findings)\n\n**Verdict: request changes.** 5 findings block the merge, 20 should be fixed or ticketed, and 14 can be ignored for now.\n\n## Rules I applied\n\n`scores.agent_risk` and `scores.severity` don't track each other here. The god function has severity 0.9 but agent_risk 0.13. The clock reads have agent_risk 0.45 but severity 0.6. So I used both:\n\n- **Block:** severity ≥ 0.75 **and** agent_risk ≥ 0.3. This means real damage that an agent is likely to spread.\n- **Block (override):** medium findings that are certain to break every environment except one developer's machine. These are the two I applied it to.\n- **Warn:** medium or high severity that isn't blocked, **or** low severity with agent_risk ≥ 0.35.\n- **Ignore:** low severity **and** agent_risk < 0.35.\n\n## 🛑 Block merge (5)\n\n| ID | Finding | Sev / agent_risk | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 00012 | `Invoice` declared twice (`api/state.ts` vs `billing.ts`), 6 fields disagree | high 0.96 / 0.37 | The worst finding. The two copies disagree on money fields (`subtotalCents`, `taxCents`, `discountCents`, `currency`), on `userId` and on `createdAt`. No build step checks one against the other, and an agent editing one copy won't update the other. |\n| 00011 | `User` declared twice, `createdAt` missing from one | high 0.90 / 0.37 | Same problem as 00012, on a timestamp field. Fix both in one change. |\n| 00005 | Variable `d` uses `getUTCFullYear()` (L9) and `getMonth()` (L41) | high 0.80 / 0.39 | The result is silently wrong by the host's UTC offset. Around month boundaries the year and month can come from different days. |\n| 00018 | Hardcoded `/Users/andrew/dev/crimes/schema.json` in `api/files.ts:9` | medium 0.60 / 0.31 *(override)* | Confidence 0.9. The path exists on one laptop, so CI, deploys and every other developer will fail. It also leaks a username. |\n| 00017 | Hardcoded `localhost:3000` in `api/files.ts:8` | medium 0.60 / 0.31 *(override)*